{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-17104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the definite integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{{(2-{x}^{3})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-17104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =2-{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =-3{x}^{2} \\\\ \\text{d}u & =-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u & ={x}^{2}\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=2-{x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{(2-{x}^{3})}^{3}}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{2}^{1}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{1}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\text{d}u & =-\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{1}{u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}|}_{2}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}({1}^{5/2}-{2}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{15}(1-({2}^{5})^{1/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{15}(1-4\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}(4\\sqrt{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-17104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "09f618ba390ece96e3949660d020fde0ec7ea2f3092feb27ea2c430f5285622d"} {"question" "q-17104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-17104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{15}(4\\sqrt{2}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{15}(2\\sqrt{2}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{15}(4\\sqrt{2}+1)"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{15}(4\\sqrt{2}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}(4\\sqrt{2}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-17104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{15}(4\\sqrt{2}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-49610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the definite integral ${\\int }_{1}^{2}{(2x+1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-49610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =2x+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=2x+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 1 & 2 \\\\ u & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}{(2x+1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{3}^{5}{u}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}{u}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3}^{5}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}|}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{5}^{3}-{3}^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{125-27}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{98}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-49610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "09f618ba390ece96e3949660d020fde0ec7ea2f3092feb27ea2c430f5285622d"} {"question" "q-49610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-49610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{43}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{49}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{49}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{59}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{95}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-49610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{49}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-113747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the definite integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{3{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-113747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =3{x}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =6x \\\\ \\text{d}u & =6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u & =x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=3{x}^{2}+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-113747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "09f618ba390ece96e3949660d020fde0ec7ea2f3092feb27ea2c430f5285622d"} {"question" "q-113747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-113747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{6}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-113747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-336717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-336717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =4x-1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=4x-1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 1 & 3 \\\\ u & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{(4x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{3}^{11}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{11}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{3}^{11}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u){|}_{3}^{11} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(11)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}ln\\,(\\frac{11}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-336717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "09f618ba390ece96e3949660d020fde0ec7ea2f3092feb27ea2c430f5285622d"} {"question" "q-336717" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-336717" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}\\ln(\\frac{11}{3})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-336788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{(4x+2)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-336788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =4x+2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=4x+2.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ u & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{(4x+2)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{2}^{4}{u}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{(4x+2)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}{u}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {\\frac{1}{4}{u}^{4}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}({4}^{4}-{2}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(256-16) \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/state.json" "file_sha256" "2f9478f63781d6defdb3680bcb02cb2fbd00bcaecf8da9e66bb13d3fa56bde75"} {"question" "q-336788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066553/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "09f618ba390ece96e3949660d020fde0ec7ea2f3092feb27ea2c430f5285622d"} {"question" "q-336788" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture